01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:13,500
Shooting Fish is a 1997 British romantic crime comedy film directed by Stefan Schwartz and co-written with Richard Holmes,
starring Dan Futterman and Stuart Townsend as two con men with Kate Beckinsale as their unwilling assistant.

11
01:14:56,250 --> 01:15:02,250
The film was produced by Winchester Films and partly funded by National
Lottery money administered through the UK Arts Council.

12
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:51,000
Shooting Fish aimed to transfer well to international markets that were keen on
British films following the success of Four Weddings and a Funeral.

13
01:28:33,750 --> 01:28:39,750
The film was released in the United Kingdom on 17 October
1997 and in the United States on 1 May 1998.

14
